From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP strip unpinned PLAYER tickets from the cut

Neighbor view-distance PLAYER tickets survived stripNonUnknownTickets
because keepTicket is type-only. After relocate nobody is in the band,
but those leftover tickets held 16 corridor keys and aborted partition.
Strip PLAYER/portal tickets unless the chunk is pinned (occupant or
dimension portal). Carve stays on. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapCorridorUnload.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapCorridorUnload.java
@@ -264,8 +264,12 @@
                 }
                 boolean progress = false;
                 for (final net.minecraft.server.level.Ticket ticket : tickets) {
-                    if (YapRegionizerGap.keepTicket(ticket.getType())) {
+                    // Keep PLAYER/portal tickets only on a pinned chunk (someone standing here,
+                    // or a nether/end portal). Neighbor VD tickets must not hold the empty buffer.
+                    if (YapRegionizerGap.keepTicket(ticket.getType())
+                            && YapRegionizerGap.pinnedChunk(world, cx, cz)) {
                         continue;
                     }
                     try {
                         final Object id = ((ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.ticket.ChunkSystemTicket<?>) ticket)
